  "description": "The Donau–Moldau cycle route runs 64 km from Haidmühle, by the Czech border, down through Neureichenau, Jandelsbrunn, Breitenberg and Wegscheid to Obernzell on the Danube, descending from about 870 m to 290 m. Half of it is on quiet minor roads, with cycle paths and short stretches of path between. The route is mostly gentle, with rolling climbs of about 670 m in total. Springs, a viewpoint at Braunberg (706 m) and a youth campsite at Rannasee are mapped near the track.\n\nRoute data © OpenStreetMap contributors (ODbL). OSM relation/273702.",
